n the welfare of created beings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78ff4362898c847c88189d93e8482d38fe6af0f25cdc69fca3e49aaa0271f5d6","compact":"9b5696142667aa2a859483de222383f33f4c1ac06ab4bb140bc0dd1b27008b07","nasal":"9b5696142667aa2a859483de222383f33f4c1ac06ab4bb140bc0dd1b27008b07"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":9,"english":"Remembering his former enmity and aggrandisement, I, being extremely wrathful, in my deer shape and with my sharpened horns, darted towards him with a view to kill him, considering through my ignorance the effulgent Rāma as none other but an ascetic living in the forest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d82e50c166a675b3b2ffa0918605893675cb6a20e78d4aea32ecaa016917af19","compact":"80db578135193be86de5df5063784fc579e024e4bfe21d571bb53e1e19ed1583","nasal":"80db578135193be86de5df5063784fc579e024e4bfe21d571bb53e1e19ed1583"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":10,"english":"Remembering his former enmity and aggrandisement, I, being extremely wrathful, in my deer shape and with my sharpened horns, darted towards him with a view to kill him, considering through my ignorance the effulgent Rāma as none other but an ascetic living in the forest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dab15597de1186fa57d5efb4b54e5be75ba003ba2822e1adfcced0a816a657ca","compact":"6092ba940797b31c6ec01183de0e4f7b7831f7c945f976bfc1d3cccd39eb5d31","nasal":"dea6883649b5d7d0546e3ac6ace58caa9cc4fa6693e69e85e81794981dfb2182"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":11,"english":"Then stringing his huge bow he darted three sharpened arrows at me. Those three terrible arrows with bent knots resembling thunderbolts, killing enemies and drinking blood and having the motion of Garuda and air, coalescing with each other came before us.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.552,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9336a9bfe4e914b18122fe1c4784edc04ad364728ccf9b3609e958e1061e9376","compact":"4da83666859917bef2db1e06094bcf3bb2847f9b2a2556521243d85fa31247a1","nasal":"4da83666859917bef2db1e06094bcf3bb2847f9b2a2556521243d85fa31247a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":12,"english":"Then stringing his huge bow he darted three sharpened arrows at me. Those three terrible arrows with bent knots resembling thunderbolts, killing enemies and drinking blood and having the motion of Garuda and air, coalescing with each other came before us.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"48460367b513dc1184b823858b34dd376b1deceedd5fc30245ad359b30c9fd7b","compact":"232f1cbd81f9b8f13fb1784e1542eeb0078876d57fdf4296b59b268152fc56a8","nasal":"232f1cbd81f9b8f13fb1784e1542eeb0078876d57fdf4296b59b268152fc56a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":13,"english":"Wicked as I am, I was fully aware of his prowess having been frightened by him on a former occasion, and so I saved myself by escaping, but those two Raksasas were killed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fa1c1bd28c62110479e5ecd790073dbd83158c2c1fb56337b66ed662fb7dce1","compact":"b80326052c029b5046ffc0a2353847f2d0950df874557e982f21fb04c4a4a78d","nasal":"3269f94ac473b82961ced069a771a4822e8703318df80361ffb1733533bd1920"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":14,"english":"O Rāvana, any how saved from the arrows of Rāma and having got my life back I have resorted to the life of an ascetic and have been carrying on asceticism here being absorbed in Yoga.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"72de102848834f70c1b3427bdabf46bf769053e9247475ace2bec25401da5a9c","compact":"e2b70dac3667089a18b381b136ffaac67a037816fe54a962e7df8f61c417b441","nasal":"e2b70dac3667089a18b381b136ffaac67a037816fe54a962e7df8f61c417b441"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":15,"english":"From that very day I see Rāma wearing bark and deerskin even in the very trees before me like to Death with the noose in his hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20f5c435b69aae3f3d5b82e7e8154b98b5a95b7524483519f684842b1ca205c6","compact":"0b9818e3a29854350360913c03b5324e6d1adfa2ba207254913ff4db66e2722e","nasal":"dbf6aaa986f31b4fd95b8f06a4d6342989d36cf8245b50bb74ebab786865550a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":16,"english":"Terrified as I am I always see thousands of Rāma around me. Me seems the entire forest is inhabited by Rāma only.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5b446797681e090c24db191c65e137873d9bb43c5d5876abbaede82caad76d27","compact":"1990a22004cc63da06d5ff98cd83ab5172b9ef67fa36075e88487cf850ffefa9","nasal":"1990a22004cc63da06d5ff98cd83ab5172b9ef67fa36075e88487cf850ffefa9"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":17,"english":"O king of Räksasas, I see Rāma even in the quarter where there is no Rāma. Seeing him in my dreams even I look around like one awaken.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a348a3e6175b8b0d8a105db986db192ec07efd5503dddb56841ab9deceaf7148","compact":"68bd4b22e8698b78566cf7fe552752bbe2698e273a860c978b8ef21c313477f7","nasal":"68bd4b22e8698b78566cf7fe552752bbe2698e273a860c978b8ef21c313477f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":18,"english":"O Rāvana what more shall I speak to you, I am so much afraid of Rāma that such words as Ratna (jewel), Ratha (chariot) which begin with the letter Ra administer consternation to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.772,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7d9f3990ce4aaecf18802e2dac052b8e8494503516ca5057e999ebc8829a280b","compact":"e9e9ecd56a1b1321a0eb797f5f8745d1b76d3a8cf116fb0c457ab97ea0c462a0","nasal":"41915df9610641f46c5c127611ecc2a4bb0bb2086e0a799522d329c63b35596d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":19,"english":"I am fully apprised of the prowess of that descendant of Raghu; it dose not behove you to enter into conflict with him; he can destroy Vāli and Namuci. O Rāvana, whether do you fight with Rāma or not, do not mention him to me if do you wish to see me.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.361,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-14","DUTT-3-39-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b6bcd1dbfe1e1203dc7f7fc68ced275ec501d6980c19c6f5d9cea4e0d7d2b93","compact":"5e1024d15adf21e1654f5d2e9d864adf7dbeacef67284606cad8e9f81a2fb3e1","nasal":"5e1024d15adf21e1654f5d2e9d864adf7dbeacef67284606cad8e9f81a2fb3e1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-37-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":37,"verse":20,"english":"You are my friend; it is for this and for your welfare that I speak this truth to you. If do you not follow my words, yourself with all your kinsmen, shall be slain in battle by Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-39-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3037020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1895042c9b2386bc0b4dcd683b8a916353fac380da70eda401223384eb798724","compact":"b8634a734e5ce01402bbefed7eafeae89de8474ba1e31d4a61199c37e6788dbe","nasal":"400c7fe75611b3811b4e271b78c6ee9babe5cf0c87c1798e9de6a3a793d990a0"}}]
